@title A Letter About Elm Street
@subtitle Corbel & Finch Books
@author Marguerite Pell, Owner

Dear friends,

For 17 years, the Elm Street shop has been a home for us and, we hope, for you. We are writing to tell you that it is closing, and to explain why.

## What is changing

The Elm Street shop will close for good after trading on 2026-12-23.

Our Harbor Road shop, our online shop and our school book fairs all continue.

## Why

When our Elm Street lease renews on 2027-01-01, the rent will rise by 70%. At the same time, more than half of our sales now happen at Harbor Road or online.

We are a family business, and we had to make a choice. We chose to keep the two places that are growing. It was not an easy decision, and we did not make it lightly.

## What stays the same

- **The same faces.** All 6 of our Elm Street booksellers are moving to Harbor Road.
- **Your gift certificates and store credit** are honored at Harbor Road and online until 2027-12-31.
- **Your loyalty points** move over automatically. There is nothing you need to do.

## How to say goodbye

We would love to see you at Elm Street before we close.

step From 2026-11-28: all Elm Street stock is 20% off | 2026-11-28
step Last Saturday story hour, 11:00 | 2026-12-19
step Farewell evening with our staff and local authors, 17:00 to 20:00 | 2026-12-22
step Last day of trading at Elm Street | 2026-12-23

Thank you. Thank you for every book you bought, every story hour you brought your children to, and every recommendation you trusted us with. Elm Street was yours as much as ours, and we are grateful for every year of it.

We hope to see you at Harbor Road.

With love and thanks,

**Marguerite Pell**
Corbel & Finch Books
